# A Lennard-Jones trajectory on domains against one domain, 200 steps of
# velocity Verlet (D[distributed-migration]); the program is in
# Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir. The state of the domains is a
# md_dist.state carried by scf.for; at every step md_dist.covered decides,
# for all domains at once, whether the halo is kept or the particles migrate
# and the halo is rebuilt.
#
# The output: the number of rebuilds and 1 if it is more than none and fewer
# than the steps (both branches ran); then, each as the difference and 1 if
# it is within the tolerance, the positions (to the nearest image, against
# the edge 4.8), the velocities (against the largest component), and the
# potential, kinetic, and total energy (against the kinetic energy), and
# the change of the total energy since the start on domains and on one
# domain (against the kinetic energy; 1.9e-4 of it after 200 steps on both,
# the fluctuation of velocity Verlet at this step; bound 1e-3).
# dist-trajectory-lj-drift.test runs 2000 steps.
#
# Tolerances. In double the differences are sums in another order, grown by
# the chaos of the trajectory: measured at most 3.9e-14 of the edge for the
# positions, 1.1e-13 of the largest component for the velocities, and 1.4e-14
# of the kinetic energy for the energies, on every grid, through both
# executors; the bounds are 1e-12, 1e-11, and 1e-12. In mixed the forces of
# md_exec are in f32: the differences are those of the f32 force kernels of
# the two programs (the derivative of the energy kernel on one domain, the
# force kernel on domains), and are the same on one domain of md_dist (1 x 1
# x 1) as on 8 or 16 domains, 9.9e-7, 1.2e-5, and 1.2e-6 measured; the
# bounds are ten times those, 1e-5, 1e-4, and 1e-5.
#
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/1.0e-12/; s/VTOL/1.0e-11/; s/ETOL/1.0e-12/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Through md_exec, in double and in mixed precision.
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/1.0e-12/; s/VTOL/1.0e-11/; s/ETOL/1.0e-12/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-md-exec="functions=main" \
# RUN:     --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/1.0e-5/; s/VTOL/1.0e-4/; s/ETOL/1.0e-5/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-md-exec="functions=main" \
# RUN:     --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-precision="mode=mixed" \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-algebra --md-exec-assign-storage --convert-md-exec-to-loops \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
